------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY SCOPE  (Honesty #2 No-scope-narrowing)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web <FadeIn> is a PURE presentational MOTION WRAPPER. Its inputs are `children` + `delay` + one
display-boundary hook (useMotionPreference(400)); it renders a motion.div whose `initial`/`animate` lift +
fade the content in over 400 ms with an optional delay. There is NO fetch, NO React-Query cache, NO Promise
-> therefore NO loading / error / stale / offline branch (there is nothing to fetch, fail, age, or
disconnect from; the hosted content owns its own data states). Reproducing those generic states would
FABRICATE behaviour the source does not have, so this surface reproduces only the source's REAL branches —
exactly the disposition the sibling presentational motion primitive StaggerItem (0194) used. The REAL
branches, all reproduced + tested:
  • full-motion entrance : initial {opacity 0, y 12} -> animate {opacity 1, y 0} over 400 ms (web duration).
  • reduced-motion       : web initial={false} -> renders in the final state {opacity 1, y 0}, no movement;
                           entrance animation nil; delay forced to 0 (web `delay: reduce ? 0 : delay`).
  • delayed entrance     : the web `delay` prop (seconds) passed to transition.delay; suppressed when
                           reduced; negative values clamped to 0.
  • empty-content leaf   : the native never-a-blank-box peer of the wrapper hosting no children.
Data source  : useMotionPreference -> FadeInMotionPreference.resolve (1:1 port; the live reduce flag binds
               via \.accessibilityReduceMotion, the native peer of useReducedMotion()).
Shared comps : none (the web source uses none).
Charts/maps  : none (the web source uses none) -> Swift Charts / MapKit not required.
i18n keys    : none in source (anonymous); only native a11y additions, resolved through the P1/S10 facade.
Telemetry    : view.opened emitted once with slug "FadeIn" (P1/S11).
a11y         : reduce-motion honored (the core behaviour, tested); Dynamic Type via tokens; the wrapper is
               VoiceOver-transparent (adds no traits, leaving content semantics intact); the empty leaf is a
               single combined, labelled element. No interactive elements (vacuous for "label on every
               interactive element").
Web-vs-native delta (Honesty #9 No-silent-drift): the web `className` prop is a Tailwind passthrough with no
native peer — a SwiftUI caller styles `FadeIn { … }` directly with modifiers — so it is intentionally
dropped (documented in FadeInInput). The easeOut entrance curve matches the web `transition.ease: 'easeOut'`.

